{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0luZGlhbl9CYW5nbGEvMjAyMC0tQmVmb3JlL0Jpa3JhbSUyMFNpbmdoYSUyMFRoZSUyMExpb24lMjBJcyUyMEJhY2slMjAlMjgyMDEyJTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Bikram Singha The Lion Is Back","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/k9BPZwcOw0qI7l1bZhPvauGDEo9.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/qGpbuwpGfILLBFAeiqi0VrUU09m.jpg","description":"Gupi (Prosenjit Chatterjee) is a small-time conman in love with Madhu (Richa Gangopadhyay), a pretty woman whom he met at a wedding he wasn't invited to. Into this picture, the world enters six-year-old Osmita (Baby Titli), who inexplicably believes Gupi to be her dad. And if this wasn't bad enough, Gupi becomes the object of a series of life-threatening attacks by a gang of criminals who seem to know something he doesn't.  While trying desperately to save his life and love, Gupi stumbles upon a deadly secret. A secret that will take him to a small town named Debgarh: A town terrorized by its ruthless MLA and the mafia he controls; a town whose inhabitants' only hope for redemption is Gupi.  Later, he learns that ACP Bikram Singha Roy (Prosenjit Chatterjee), his look alike, is in danger from criminals.\n\nReleased 24 May 2012 · India · Language: Bengali · 130 min\nStudio: Eskay Movies\n\nOn your server — Audio: Bengali","releaseInfo":"2012","genres":["Action","Bengali"],"imdbRating":"6.9","runtime":"130 min","cast":["Prosenjit Chatterjee","Richa Gangopadhyay","Supriyo Dutta","Besant Ravi","Maheck Chahal","Sabyasachi Chakraborty","Sanjib Sarkar","Parthasarathi Chakraborty"],"director":["Rajiv Kumar"],"released":"2012-05-24T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Rajiv Kumar","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/6zB4B0yh59QrwTYoBKPZ9Ba0Mwd.jpg"},{"name":"Prosenjit Chatterjee","character":"Goopy / Bikram Singha","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/vtXVSJebnsmfJC38gPy76QN3JTo.jpg"},{"name":"Richa Gangopadhyay","photo":"https://image.tmdb.